<title>UK: Lithuania sets $200 mln five-year bond.</title>
<headline>Lithuania sets $200 mln five-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager J.P. Morgan.</p>
<p> BORROWER   LITHUANIA</p>
<p> AMT    $200 MLN	COUPON     **	  MATURITY    22.JUL.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  **	  PAY DATE    22.JUL.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.625     REOFFER    **	  SPREAD	+105 BP</p>
<p> NOTES   ** TO BE PRICED</p>
<p> MOODY	BA2	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  BBB-	DENOMS (K) 10+1	SALE LIMITS US/UK/LI</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   IPMA 1</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  LITHUANIA TAX PROVS   GROSS UP</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.375     SELL CONC  0.25	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.25 PCT JUNE 2002 U.S. TREASURY NOTE</p>
<p> NOTES	144A ELIGIBLE</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
